From 9f3c1d90607740fae320bc8e05107f67bb579c10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexaInc <rasanjanahansaka2006@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:46:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(firmware): unblock manual capture, live OLED status
 screen and logo boot animation

- cap_photo in MANUAL mode (no active mission) no longer requires GPS or a
  mapped crop block: the robot stops, centers the camera servo and captures
  one 'manual' photo; the server resolves or stores the block context.
  Autonomous waypoint scans keep the both-sides capture behavior.
- captureAndUploadImage never aborts with 'Capture blocked' anymore; empty
  plant/blockId fields are simply omitted from the upload.
- JMD0.96D-1 (SSD1306 128x64) display no longer sticks on 'Initializing...':
  it now plays a CropHealth logo boot animation (sprout grow + pulse rings +
  typed brand line), shows per-stage boot progress (hardware/WiFi/server) and
  then a live 1 Hz status screen: WiFi state + IP, WebSocket state, GPS fix,
  satellites and MANUAL/AUTO/PAUSED/CAPTURING mode.
- logo_bitmap.h (generated from the shared brand logo) added next to every
  sketch copy; applied identically to src/main.cpp, sketch.ino and
  arduino-ide/esp32-dev-controller/esp32-dev-controller.ino.
- Wokwi precompiled firmware.bin/.elf rebuilt (pio run, flash 78.6%).
